# Headers for the static web build (Cloudflare / Netlify `_headers` format).
# Expo copies public/ into dist/ on `expo export`.
#
# SUPABASE_PROJECT_HOST below is a placeholder for the Supabase project's host
# name (the `abcdefgh.supabase.co` part of EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL, with no
# https:// and no path). Deploy with `npm run build:web`: it exports the app
# and then writes the real host into dist/_headers from
# EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL (scripts/apply-web-headers.js), and fails if the
# placeholder is still there. Never edit the placeholder in this file. If it
# reaches production unreplaced the app cannot reach the backend at all, so
# the mistake is obvious and nothing is exposed. See docs/OPERATIONS.md.
#
# Content-Security-Policy, verified against the real export (2026-11-12):
# - script-src 'self': the export has one external script and no inline
#   script, and runs without eval. zod probes `new Function("")` once at
#   start-up, is refused, and falls back; that shows as one console report
#   per page load and is harmless. Do not add 'unsafe-eval' to silence it.
# - style-src 'unsafe-inline': react-native-web and expo-font inject <style>
#   elements at run time.
# - connect-src data: blob: is for reading a picked image before upload
#   (lib/images.ts fetches the picker's blob:/data: URI).
# - wss:// is for Supabase Realtime, which the app does not use yet.
/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: blob: https://SUPABASE_PROJECT_HOST; font-src 'self' data:; connect-src 'self' data: blob: https://SUPABASE_PROJECT_HOST wss://SUPABASE_PROJECT_HOST; manifest-src 'self'; worker-src 'self'; frame-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; object-src 'none'
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=()
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin-allow-popups
  Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: same-origin

# Caching. These paths never overlap, because hosts join a header that two
# matching rules both set. File names under /_expo/static and /assets carry a
# content hash, so they can be cached for a year. The page itself must be
# revalidated on every visit so a new deploy is picked up; deep links
# (/discover and so on) are served the same index.html with the host's
# default, which is already "max-age=0, must-revalidate".
/_expo/static/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/index.html
  Cache-Control: no-cache
